        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "58917b53-1a07-532f-97a0-8562f9529a79",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies, St. Olaf College\n- People: Michael Bauman, Bernt Julius Muus, Thorbjorn N. Mohn\n- Places: Oxford\n- Topics: American colleges and universities connected to CMRS\n\nFacts:\n- St. Olaf College was founded in 1874 by Norwegian-American immigrant pastors and farmers led by Pastor Bernt Julius Muus.\n- Thorbjorn N. Mohn, who lived from July 15, 1844 to November 18, 1899, was an American Lutheran church leader and the first president of St. Olaf College.\n- Michael Bauman served for eight years as Lecturer and Tutor in Renaissance theology and literature at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies in Oxford.\n- Michael Bauman also served as Associate Dean of the Summer School at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies.\n- Among the American colleges and universities that sent students to the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies were the University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, and Middlebury College.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "31911d63-9750-5870-aacc-9b067bb5ea3a",
        "text": "Page: Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies. Sentence: Among the American colleges and universities that have sent students to CMRS are The University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, Middlebury College.\nPage: St. Olaf College. Sentence: It was founded in 1874 by a group of Norwegian-American immigrant pastors and farmers, led by Pastor Bernt Julius Muus.\nPage: Michael Bauman. Sentence: He was for eight years Lecturer and Tutor in Renaissance theology and Literature at the Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies, Oxford, where he also was Associate Dean of the Summer School.\nPage: Thorbjorn N. Mohn. Sentence: Thorbjorn N. Mohn (July 15, 1844 - November 18, 1899) was an American Lutheran church leader and the first president of St. Olaf College.",
